---
source: crates/ambers-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: "ok_stdout(&[\"open\", \"--help\"])"
---
Open a file in your browser

Starts a small server on this machine (127.0.0.1 only), prints its address and opens it in the browser. The page asks only for the rows it shows, so a file of any size opens at once. Without a file, the page lists the data files of the folder to pick from. If ambers is already serving, the file is opened there instead of starting a second server. Ctrl+C stops the server; it also stops by itself a few minutes after the last page is closed.

Usage: ambers open [OPTIONS] [FILE|FOLDER]

Arguments:
  [FILE|FOLDER]
          A .sav or .zsav file to open, or a folder to list
          
          With a folder, or with nothing (the current folder), the page lists the data files found there and opens the one you pick.

Options:
      --port <PORT>
          Port to listen on (default: 2627, or the next free one after it)

      --no-browser
          Only print the address; do not open the browser

      --keep-alive
          Keep serving after the last page is closed

      --limit <N>
          Load at most N rows (the rest of a larger file is not read)

      --memory <GB>
          Load at most this many GB of data into memory
          
          By default loading stops at half of the memory the machine has free when the file is opened. The rows already loaded stay usable.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
